<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Mu of Qin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 621 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ying Renhao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Mu of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> from 659 to 621 BCE and is often listed among the Five Hegemons of the Spring and Autumn period. He employed able foreign ministers, helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-wen-of-jin">Chong'er</a> of Jin take power and expanded Qin westward over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong peoples</a>. He was said to have mourned when Chu destroyed the state of Jiang in 623 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-mu-of-qin.jpg" alt="Duke Mu of Qin" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 馮夢龍 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%A7%A6%E7%A9%86%E5%85%AC_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E6%9D%B1%E5%91%A8%E5%88%97%E5%9C%8B%E5%85%A8%E5%BF%97.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
